@startuml usecase
' Use Case Diagram - Colors web application (Labs 1-3)
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
title Colors application - user goals
left to right direction

actor User
actor "MySQL Database" as DB <<supporting system>>

rectangle "Colors Web Application (browser + PHP)" {
  usecase "Log In" as UC_Login
  usecase "Search Colors" as UC_Search
  usecase "Add Color" as UC_Add
  usecase "Log Out" as UC_Logout
  usecase "Show Login Error" as UC_LoginErr
}

User -- UC_Login
User -- UC_Search
User -- UC_Add
User -- UC_Logout

UC_LoginErr ..> UC_Login : <<extend>>\n[response.id < 1]

UC_Login -- DB
UC_Search -- DB
UC_Add -- DB

legend bottom
  Log In: POST Login.php {login, password}; a matching row leads to color.html.
  One firstName cookie stores firstName,lastName,userId and expires in 20 minutes.
  Search Colors: POST SearchColors.php {search, userId}; LIKE pattern is "%" + search + "%".
  Search filters by the supplied userId.
  Add Color: POST AddColor.php {color, userId}.
  Log Out: reset browser user state, expire the cookie, and return to index.html.
  On color.html load only, readCookie() restores state and redirects if userId < 0.
  Search and Add do not include a session verification step.
  The PHP endpoints trust the supplied userId; no server session is verified.
  Error paths are detailed in activity.puml.
  No registration, edit, or delete features exist in the app.
end legend
@enduml
